 ### Activity
 
 Every change to a list or its tasks adds an entry `{ "id", "action", "task_id", "user", "detail", "created_at" }`.
 Actions: `list.created`, `list.renamed`, `task.created`, `task.updated` (`detail.changes` names the fields that
-changed), `task.deleted`, `comment.added`.
+changed), `task.deleted`, `comment.added`, `member.joined` and `member.removed` (`detail.role`).
+
+## Sharing
+
+A list has its owner and members, each member being an `editor` or a `viewer`.
+
+| | owner | editor | viewer |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| read the list, its tasks, comments, tags, activity and members | yes | yes | yes |
+| create, change and delete tasks; comment | yes | yes | no |
+| rename or delete the list | yes | no | no |
+| create and revoke invitations, see the pending ones, remove members | yes | no | no |
+
+| Method and path | Body | Answers |
+|---|---|---|
+| `POST /api/lists/:id/invitations` | `{ "role": "viewer" \| "editor", "expires_in_hours"? }` | 201 `{ "id", "token", "url", "role", "expires_at" }`; `expires_in_hours` is above 0 and at most 720, 72 by default |
+| `GET /api/lists/:id/invitations` | | 200, the pending invitations `[{ "id", "role", "created_at", "expires_at" }]` (without token) |
+| `DELETE /api/lists/:id/invitations/:invitationId` | | 204: the link stops working |
+| `POST /api/invitations/:token/accept` | | 200, the list (with the caller's `role`); 404 if the invitation is unknown, revoked or used, 410 if it expired |
+| `GET /api/lists/:id/members` | | 200, `[{ "id", "username", "role" }]`, the owner first, with the role `owner` |
+| `DELETE /api/lists/:id/members/:userId` | | 204; 400 for the owner; 404 for someone who is not a member |
+
+- The `url` of an invitation is `<origin>/#invitation=<token>`. The origin is `PUBLIC_URL` if that environment
+  variable is set, else the `Host` of the request. The token is in the fragment so that it is not sent to servers,
+  nor in referrers. Opening the link shows the page; once the person is signed in (or has created an account) the
+  page accepts the invitation and shows the list.
+- The token is shown once, when the invitation is created: only its hash is stored. An invitation is used once: the
+  first signed-in user who accepts it becomes a member, and it no longer is pending. The owner accepting their own
+  invitation changes nothing; a member keeps their role, except a viewer who accepts an editor invitation and
+  becomes an editor.
+- Access is checked on every request: a removed member loses it at once. Removing a member unassigns their tasks
+  in the list (and cancels their reminders). Deleting a list deletes its members and invitations.
+- A task can be assigned to the owner or to any member of its list.
 
